[UTCTime "15:06:27"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

4... Bd7 { They play this with the main focus of attacking our queen.
The move is obvious you don't even need my help } 5. Qxc4 { Yessir } 5... Nc6 { Now develop like normal chess } { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gb1c3] } 6. Nc3 Nf6 7. e4 Bb4 { Now play the move Bd3 to defend the pawn } 8. Bd3 O-O { Kick da bishop! } 9. a3 Bxc3+ 10. Qxc3 a6 { Now pin the knight } 11. Bg5 h6 { [%csl Gh4][%cal Gg5h4] } 12. Bh4 g5 { [%csl Gg3][%cal Gh4g3] } 13. Bg3 Re8 { Now we can castle kingside or queenside and attack the knights with e5 } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Ge4e5,Re1h1,Be1a1] } *


