4... c6 { This is the pawn's defence, just take like always } 5. Qxc4 Nf6 { Now you do not have to worry about the Bb4 pin cause the pawn on c3 blocks the b1 knight's square, so play Nc3! } 6. Nc3 { Now we have a nice position we're plannig to play e4 next and develop so we can castle } *


